      "source": [
        "# Recession Impact Analysis\n",
        "## Predictive Modeling & Future Hypothesis\n",
        "\n",
        "Tests whether recession indicators can forecast sector job losses.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Hook #5:** If a recession hits tomorrow, which cohort faces a steeper percentage wipeout—and how many months to recover?\n",
        "\n",
        "---\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: Load tools and data\n",
        "\n",
        "Reads `master_table.csv` from Notebook 1.\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 12,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "Loaded 1054 rows x 11 columns\n",
            "Date range: 1939-01-31 to 2026-10-31\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "import os\n",
        "import sklearn\n",
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
        "from sklearn.linear_model import LinearRegression\n",
        "from sklearn.metrics import mean_squared_error, r2_score\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.rcParams[\"figure.figsize\"] = (12, 5)\n",
        "\n",
        "df = pd.read_csv(os.path.join(\"..\", \"data\", \"processed\", \"master_table.csv\"),\n",
        "                 parse_dates=[\"date\"], index_col=\"date\").sort_index()\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"Loaded {df.shape[0]} rows x {df.shape[1]} columns\")\n",
        "print(f\"Date range: {df.index.min().date()} to {df.index.max().date()}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: Feature engineering\n",
        "\n",
        "Targets: forward 12-month % change for blue_collar_jobs and white_collar_jobs.\n",
        "Features: recession indicator, lagged employment levels, lagged ratios.\n",
        "Time-based split: first 80% train, last 20% test.\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 13,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "Model-ready: 1030 rows x 23 columns\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "emp_cols = [\"blue_collar_jobs\", \"white_collar_jobs\"]\n",
        "model_df = df.copy()\n",
        "\n",
        "# Forward 12-month % change targets\n",
        "for col in emp_cols:\n",
        "    model_df[f\"{col}_fwd12_pct\"] = model_df[col].shift(-12) / model_df[col] - 1\n",
        "\n",
        "# Lagged features\n",
        "for col in emp_cols:\n",
        "    for lag in [1, 3, 6, 12]:\n",
        "        model_df[f\"{col}_lag{lag}\"] = model_df[col].shift(lag)\n",
        "\n",
        "model_df[\"recession_indicator\"] = df[\"recession_indicator\"]\n",
        "model_df[\"white_collar_pct_lag1\"] = df[\"white_collar_pct\"].shift(1)\n",
        "model_df[\"blue_collar_pct_lag1\"] = df[\"blue_collar_pct\"].shift(1)\n",
        "\n",
        "model_df = model_df.dropna()\n",
        "print(f\"Model-ready: {model_df.shape[0]} rows x {model_df.shape[1]} columns\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: Train models\n",
        "\n",
        "One linear regression per cohort. Time-respecting split (no shuffling).\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 17,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "\n",
            "=== Blue Collar Jobs ===\n",
            "Train R² : 0.4215\n",
            "Test R²  : -4.9525   (correct order: y_test, y_pred)\n",
            "RMSE     : 0.0821\n",
            "Recession coef: -0.0464\n",
            "\n",
            "=== White Collar Jobs ===\n",
            "Train R² : 0.3353\n",
            "Test R²  : -0.7612   (correct order: y_test, y_pred)\n",
            "RMSE     : 0.0395\n",
            "Recession coef: -0.0305\n",
            "\n",
            "=== MODEL RESULTS ===\n",
            "\n",
            "  rmse  Out-of-Sample Test R²  Train R²  recession_coef  train_n  test_n\n",
            "0.0821                -4.9525    0.4215         -0.0464      824     206\n",
            "0.0395                -0.7612    0.3353         -0.0305      824     206\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: Regression Models — Forward 12-Month % Change Targets\n",
        "\"\"\"\n",
        "Train/test split is strictly time-ordered (first 80% train, last 20% test).\n",
        "Target = forward 12-month % change in employment.\n",
        "Features = lagged employment levels + lagged ratios + recession indicator.\n",
        "\"\"\"\n",
        "\n",
        "from sklearn.linear_model import LinearRegression\n",
        "from sklearn.metrics import mean_squared_error, r2_score\n",
        "\n",
        "emp_cols = [\"blue_collar_jobs\", \"white_collar_jobs\"]\n",
        "\n",
        "# Use SIMPLER features: just recession indicator + 1-month lag (less noise)\n",
        "feature_cols = [\n",
        "    \"recession_indicator\",\n",
        "    \"blue_collar_jobs_lag1\",\n",
        "    \"white_collar_jobs_lag1\",\n",
        "    \"white_collar_pct_lag1\",\n",
        "    \"blue_collar_pct_lag1\",\n",
        "]\n",
        "\n",
        "results = []\n",
        "\n",
        "for col in emp_cols:\n",
        "    target = f\"{col}_fwd12_pct\"\n",
        "    model_data = model_df[feature_cols + [target]].dropna()\n",
        "    \n",
        "    if len(model_data) == 0:\n",
        "        print(f\"⚠️ No valid data for {col}\")\n",
        "        continue\n",
        "    \n",
        "    X = model_data[feature_cols]\n",
        "    y = model_data[target]\n",
        "    \n",
        "    # STRICT time split: first 80% train, last 20% test. NO SHUFFLE.\n",
        "    split_idx = int(len(X) * 0.8)\n",
        "    X_train, X_test = X.iloc[:split_idx], X.iloc[split_idx:]\n",
        "    y_train, y_test = y.iloc[:split_idx], y.iloc[split_idx:]\n",
        "    \n",
        "    # Fit model\n",
        "    model = LinearRegression()\n",
        "    model.fit(X_train, y_train)\n",
        "    \n",
        "    # Predict on TEST only\n",
        "    y_pred = model.predict(X_test)\n",
        "    \n",
        "    # CORRECT r2_score order: y_true first, y_pred second\n",
        "    r2_test = r2_score(y_test, y_pred)\n",
        "    rmse = np.sqrt(mean_squared_error(y_test, y_pred))\n",
        "    recession_coef = model.coef_[0]\n",
        "    \n",
        "    # Train R² to check overfitting\n",
        "    r2_train = r2_score(y_train, model.predict(X_train))\n",
        "    \n",
        "    results.append({\n",
        "        \"cohort\": col,\n",
        "        \"rmse\": round(rmse, 4),\n",
        "        \"Out-of-Sample Test R²\": round(r2_test, 4),\n",
        "        \"Train R²\": round(r2_train, 4),\n",
        "        \"recession_coef\": round(recession_coef, 4),\n",
        "        \"train_n\": len(X_train),\n",
        "        \"test_n\": len(X_test)\n",
        "    })\n",
        "    \n",
        "    print(f\"\\n=== {col.replace('_', ' ').title()} ===\")\n",
        "    print(f\"Train R² : {r2_train:.4f}\")\n",
        "    print(f\"Test R²  : {r2_test:.4f}   (correct order: y_test, y_pred)\")\n",
        "    print(f\"RMSE     : {rmse:.4f}\")\n",
        "    print(f\"Recession coef: {recession_coef:.4f}\")\n",
        "\n",
        "results_df = pd.DataFrame(results)\n",
        "print(\"\\n=== MODEL RESULTS ===\\n\")\n",
        "print(results_df.set_index(\"cohort\").to_string(index=False))\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### Step 5: Recovery duration analysis\n",
        "\n",
        "Historical table: how many months until employment returns to pre-recession peak,\n",
        "by cohort and by recession.\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 18,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "Distinct recession episodes found: 13\n",
            "\n",
            "=== RECOVERY DURATION SUMMARY (Months to Return to Pre-Recession Peak) ===\n",
            "\n",
            "      Cohort  Avg Months  Min Months  Max Months  N Episodes\n",
            " blue_collar   57.454545        19.0       226.0          11\n",
